Proposal builder:
```
def propose(row):
    for field in ('evidence_url','url','doi','arxiv_id'):
        val = row.get(field,'').strip()
        if not val: continue
        if field=='doi':
            cand = 'https://doi.org/'+val
        elif field=='arxiv_id':
            cand = 'https://arxiv.org/abs/'+val
        else:
            cand = val
        if is_single_record(cand): return field, cand
    return None, None
```
is_single_record rejects search_query/'?q='/ '/api/literature?q=' and '...' and empty.

Fetching:
- route by host:
  - export.arxiv.org/api/query?id_list=... → parse Atom XML (title, authors, published, id) using xml.etree.
  - arxiv.org/abs/ID → parse HTML for `<meta name="citation_title" content="...">`, `citation_author`, `citation_date`.
  - inspirehep.net/api/literature/<recid> → JSON: metadata.titles[0].title, metadata.authors[].full_name, metadata.publication_info[0].year, metadata.dois, metadata.arxiv_eprints.
  - api.crossref.org/works/<doi> → JSON message.title[0], author, issued.
  - doi.org/<doi> → landing HTML with citation_title meta.
- Actually for proposals we only need INSPIRE API and arXiv abs. Controls need crossref + doi.org maybe. Keep routes for crossref too.

Title match:
```
def title_match(a,b):
    na,nb = norm(a), norm(b)
    if not na or not nb: return False,'EMPTY'
    if na==nb: return True,'EXACT'
    if na in nb or nb in na: return True,'CONTAINMENT'
    f1 = token_f1(na,nb)
    return (f1>=0.75), f'TOKEN_F1_{f1:.3f}'
```

Also record author match and year (advisory) for corroboration.

